WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.601
-Thanks so much for coming back
on the show.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.367
-So happy to be here.
Hey, guys, how you doing?

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.968
I just realized
I forgot to wear a shirt.

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:09.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.834
-I just realized --

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:14.133
I just realized that I
remembered to wear a shirt.

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:16.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:17.501
That's usually my look.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:21.434
-Next time, we can trade off.
-Oh, how sad would that be.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.000
Before we get into "Morbius,"
by the way,

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.734
I'm so psyched to talk to you
about that.

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:26.701
It is Nana Week here
at the show.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:29.000
And I have a photo here of you

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.767
bringing your Grandma Ruby
to a premiere in 2004.

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:34.300
[ Audience aws ]
-Yeah.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
Grandma Ruby.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.834
-A little cheek pinch
right there.

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:41.634
-She got a hold, didn't let go.
-Yeah.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:45.234
But you were telling me that
your Oscar-winning performance

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:48.200
in "Dallas Buyers Club,"
you took some of her mannerisms.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.901
-You know what?
She had a heart of gold.

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:52.701
She was like the quintessential
Southern grandmother.

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:55.367
And when she wasn't chasing me
around with a fly swatter --

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:57.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.634
-She did?

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.934
-Don't act like you've never
been schooled by your grandma.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:05.434
-Yeah, that's what grandmas do.
-I learned a lot of lessons.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:06.868
-Of course,
that's what Grandma does.

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:08.234
-She wasn't afraid to teach me.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.567
But actually, you know,
what's funny is

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.934
she was the first person --

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:14.200
I saw the original "Dracula"
because of her.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.834
I was up late at night.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:18.801
There was a giant cockroach
that ran across my neck.

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:20.934
That's another story.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:23.868
I was sleeping on the floor,
which you do when you're a kid.

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:26.000
-Of course.
-That's normal.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.534
-I do it as an adult.

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:29.534
[ Laughter ]
Depends on what night it is.

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:31.367
-You never know what you're
gonna find down there.

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:34.100
But yeah, a cockroach, it was a
crazy thing. It was hysterical.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.701
But anyway, I was up.

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:39.033
And she let me stay up and watch
the original "Dracula" with her.

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:41.534
And that's when I fell in love
with vampires.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.501
Yeah. True story.
-Wow. No way.

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:45.367
-Yeah. Grandma Ruby!

00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:47.267
-Grandma Ruby, shout-out to her,
yeah!

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:48.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:51.434
I want to get into "Morbius,"
but first,

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:54.334
your show "WeCrashed" started
streaming earlier

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:56.634
this month on Apple TV+.
-Whoo!

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.767
-Everyone is talking about it.
You're trending every other day.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:01.434
-I appreciate that one bit of
applause. That was very nice.

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:03.467
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, that one person.

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:05.667
Yeah. But it is.

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:06.767
People are talking about this.

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:08.400
-Yeah. It's a fun one.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.400
-It's a real story.
-Yeah.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.934
-You play a real guy,
Adam Neumann.

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:16.000
-Yeah, Adam Neumann who started
a little company called WeWork

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.067
and grew it from nothing into
a $47 billion empire.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:22.367
Had a lot of success,
a lot of failure.

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:25.534
And we examined
this crazy story.

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:27.133
Really colorful character.

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:29.667
But it was a blast.
I do it with Annie Hathaway.

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:31.467
-Yeah, both of you guys
are fantastic.

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.734
-Thank you.
-Getting great reviews.

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:34.968
You get the accents down.

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:37.767
You know -- It's --
Is it an Israeli accent?

00:02:37.767 --> 00:02:39.400
-It's an Israeli accent, yeah.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.701
I had a great team of Israelis

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:45.567
helping me out and guiding me,
beating me up, coaching me.

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:47.033
-Telling you that's wrong.
-Making sure I never --

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.300
I didn't stray from the bath.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.801
-Yes.
-But they were very --

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:53.400
They weren't delicate but they
were very -- they were amazing.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.067
-Did you ever get to meet
the guy you were playing?

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.400
-You know, I did actually.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.901
I had a top-secret meeting
with him.

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:04.267
And top-secret because it was
top-secret.

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.067
-Of course.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:08.367
Say no more.
-He spilled the beans recently,

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:09.868
so now I can talk about it.

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:12.000
But I met him.
I thought he was a lovely guy.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.934
-And, well, I can tell you,
I watched "Morbius."

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:18.334
It's a giant Marvel movie,
and you're the first

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:21.100
to actually take him
from comic book to the screen.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.801
Here is Morbius right here.

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.334
Charming-looking guy.

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:26.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:29.567
He's neither good nor evil,
I would say.

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:32.334
-No, he's something in between.
-Yeah.

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:36.367
-That delicate dance
between good and evil.

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:37.868
But I like the complexity.

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:41.434
I definitely don't have
that nine-pack right there.

00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:43.934
-They did throw an extra two
or three abs in there.

00:03:43.934 --> 00:03:45.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:51.834
But you do have -- your body
goes from frail into --

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:55.100
Basically, you feel bad for you
from the first scene.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.100
I'm like rooting for you
since day one.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.934
-Yeah. I start off playing
Dr. Michael Morbius,

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:03.667
who's this brilliant scientist
and doctor who's searching for

00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:06.801
a very -- a cure
to a really rare disease.

00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:08.634
He's sick and he's frail

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:10.868
and he's really dying
before our eyes.

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:14.100
So that was incredibly
challenging.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.868
And then he becomes
strong and powerful

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:19.968
and then ultimately, monstrous.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:22.334
-Well, your character invents
an artificial blood

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:26.067
which saves so many diseases
and actually gets award-winning

00:04:26.067 --> 00:04:27.567
and you're a great guy
and that's awesome

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:30.701
that you did that, but then you
also have your own thing

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:32.534
that you're dealing with
and you go, "You know,

00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:35.634
I want to research these
vampire bats in Costa Rica

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:38.801
and let's see what they're all
about 'cause they suck the blood

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:41.000
but maybe there's a way they can
take out the blood."

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.067
And you mix it with yours.
And there's a lot of centrifuge

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:46.901
in the movie --
any fans of centrifuge.

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:48.801
You get to see that in the film.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:52.334
-As soon as those vials start
spinning, oh, man, I'm in.

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:54.300
-That's when the movie
starts going.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.000
And so, you're like,
"Maybe I can put --"

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.601
'Cause now you're
this famous doctor.

00:04:58.601 --> 00:05:02.133
"I could put
a little vampire bat blood in me

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:05.033
and maybe save me and see what
happens." You test it.

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:06.601
-It's not the worst idea
I've ever heard.

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:08.400
-No, and you've tried
different things.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.734
And you do it, and all of
a sudden, you're all-powerful.

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.334
-Yeah.
-And you can walk again.

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:14.834
-Yeah.
-And you don't need crutches.

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:16.334
And you're like,
"Oh, wait, what's going on?"

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:20.868
Then you just start turning into
a vampire, a bat.

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:22.100
-Yes.
-Frightening.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.033
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:24.234
-[ Hisses ]
-Yes.

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:25.868
-Yes. Frightening.

00:05:25.868 --> 00:05:27.434
-By the way,
that was pretty good.

00:05:27.434 --> 00:05:29.133
-Thank you, I auditioned for it.
Yeah.

00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:30.934
[ Laughter ]
I didn't get it.

00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:32.400
I auditioned to play
your little brother.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:33.734
I was like, yeah.

00:05:33.734 --> 00:05:36.200
"If there's a sequel, you know,
you can give me a call."

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.667
-I would love to see him
in a sequel, would you not?

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:41.868
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:44.167
"Here's your coffee,
Dr. Morbius."

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:45.968
-We could put a scene in there.

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:47.501
-"Here's your coffee,
Dr. Morbius."

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:50.200
-"Oh, thank you."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:54.267
-I would love to be --
But then you see what happens

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:55.467
in the movie,
and you start rooting for you

00:05:55.467 --> 00:05:56.767
And you go, "We need Morbius."

00:05:56.767 --> 00:05:58.601
-Yeah, we do.
-To stop the evil.

00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:01.667
-We need Morbius to stop
the evil, that's for sure.

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:04.968
You know what? I have to say
this is the first time

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:09.100
that I've ever starred in
a very -- a huge film like this.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.834
I've never -- My whole career,
I've made mostly

00:06:11.834 --> 00:06:13.567
independent films
and made a career

00:06:13.567 --> 00:06:14.968
out of playing smaller parts.

00:06:14.968 --> 00:06:16.968
But this is, like, the first
time I've ever starred

00:06:16.968 --> 00:06:19.234
in a big Marvel movie like this.

00:06:19.234 --> 00:06:21.267
And I'm incredibly excited.

00:06:21.267 --> 00:06:22.901
And it's the first time
that Morbius

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:24.467
has ever been on the screen.

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:26.434
So that was a big honor
to get asked

00:06:26.434 --> 00:06:28.334
to bring this character to life.

00:06:28.334 --> 00:06:30.934
-It's giant. Go see it in
the theaters. Go see it in IMAX.

00:06:30.934 --> 00:06:33.834
Get popcorn. It's loud,
it's fun, it's exciting.

00:06:33.834 --> 00:06:35.067
-Drink a little blood
if you want.

00:06:35.067 --> 00:06:38.467
-Yeah, no, no, yeah,
the right type, of course.

00:06:38.467 --> 00:06:39.767
I have to ask you about this.

00:06:39.767 --> 00:06:40.868
You don't have to
answer or anything.

00:06:40.868 --> 00:06:43.133
But you caused
a little bit of a stir,

00:06:43.133 --> 00:06:45.234
which you tend to do,

00:06:45.234 --> 00:06:47.667
but you were at the "Spider-Man:
No Way Home" premiere.

00:06:47.667 --> 00:06:49.200
-Yes.
-And you go there,

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.067
and everyone is like, "Aw, cool,
Jared Leto is awesome.

00:06:51.067 --> 00:06:52.667
He's a stud. We love this guy."

00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:56.334
And then someone zoomed in, and
you were wearing this necklace.

00:06:56.334 --> 00:06:58.801
It says just the number 6.

00:06:58.801 --> 00:07:02.901
Now, there is a way -- there's
a thing called the Sinister Six.

00:07:02.901 --> 00:07:04.501
I don't know if you heard.

00:07:04.501 --> 00:07:09.300
Morbius, Spider-Man,
just saying, things happen.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.234
This is here. You're here.

00:07:11.234 --> 00:07:12.868
What just went down right now?

00:07:12.868 --> 00:07:14.234
I showed that photo.

00:07:14.234 --> 00:07:17.033
Your reaction is
very poker face, you know?

00:07:17.033 --> 00:07:18.734
-It was actually meant
to be a 9.

00:07:18.734 --> 00:07:19.968
It just got flipped.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.968 --> 00:07:22.067
-Oh, my God.
Oh, that's what it is.

00:07:22.067 --> 00:07:24.100
Sorry about that.
Oh, now I get it.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:25.367
There you go. It's alright.

00:07:25.367 --> 00:07:27.567
There you go. I take it back.

00:07:27.567 --> 00:07:29.501
Sorry. I apologize.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.501 --> 00:07:31.200
There's no truth to that.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:34.334
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here is Jared Leto in "Morbius."

00:07:34.334 --> 00:07:35.801
Take a look at this.

00:07:35.801 --> 00:07:43.868
♪♪

00:07:43.868 --> 00:07:51.968
♪♪

00:07:51.968 --> 00:08:00.100
♪♪

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:08.200
♪♪

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:16.267
♪♪

00:08:16.267 --> 00:08:18.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, it's fun.

00:08:18.133 --> 00:08:19.634
Jared Leto, everybody!

00:08:19.634 --> 00:08:22.133
"Morbius" hits theaters
this weekend.

